Rule 1 (input tensor elements should be within the domain of arcsin [-1, 1])
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : min(v_1) ≥ -1 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 3 (output tensor should have the same shape as the input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 24 (If the 'out' tensor is provided it should have at least the same number of elements as the 'input' tensor. This is to prevent a situation that not all values can be placed)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else if ndim(v_2) = 0 then false else (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1)-1]: shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
